Chapter: EffectDottedDeny
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Lattice probe, wrong direction (effect rows stage 0). The prefix
 relation only widens a child to its parent: Console.Write is covered by
 Console, and Console is NOT covered by Console.Write. A def that declares
 the sub-effect and performs the parent must fail with CDX2031.

 The probe needs something whose effect really is the bare parent, and no
 builtin is one: every console operation is dotted, and print-line-uni
 declares Console.Write. This test used to call print-line-uni directly and
 assert its effect was the broader Console. That stopped being true when
 the builtin was narrowed, and the test then compiled clean -- it had
 become a probe whose subject satisfied it, proving nothing.

 broad supplies the parent effect honestly: it declares Console and
 performs Console.Write, which is the permitted direction. narrow then
 declares the child and performs the parent through broad, which is the
 direction that must be refused.

Section: Definitions

  broad : Text -> [Console] Nothing
  broad (t) = print-line-uni t

  narrow : Text -> [Console.Write] Nothing
  narrow (t) = broad t

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    narrow "hello"
  end
